{"id":"21.11.RhinoFuture","contentHtml":"<p>This project was created in 48 hours for the <strong>Selectel Retro Game Jam</strong>. As the leader and sole programmer in a team with a 3D modeler, I was responsible for the idea and 100% of the technical implementation.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The concept required creating a large interactive world covered with grass, which became an interesting technical challenge within strict constraints.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2>Challenge</h2>\n<p>The main challenge is to implement grass \"eating\". The world was covered with an <strong>array of grass blades</strong> rendered via <code>DrawMeshInstancedIndirect</code>. It was necessary to find a way to <strong>efficiently change the state (hide) of thousands of instances in real-time</strong> without performance drops.</p>\n<h2>Engineering Solution</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Grass \"Eating\" System on <code>Compute Shader</code>:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Grass state (eaten/not eaten) is stored in a <code>Render Texture</code>, which is used as a mask.</li>\n<li>Interaction with the world happens like this:\n<ol>\n<li>Rhino heads are drawn as simple points on a temporary texture (<code>CustomRenderTexture</code>).</li>\n<li><code>Compute Shader</code> on the GPU takes this texture with points and \"stamps\" it into the main grass mask.</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Key Scoring Optimization:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>The same <code>Compute Shader</code> <mark>simultaneously counts the number of \"eaten\" pixels</mark> and writes the result directly to a <code>Compute Buffer</code>.</li>\n<li>This allows getting points for eaten grass <strong>without the expensive operation of reading texture from GPU to CPU</strong>, which is critical for performance.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Grass Shader Modification:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>I modified the main grass shader, adding the ability to overlay a <strong>texture with a logo</strong> on top of it, which was one of the hackathon requirements.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Outcome</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>High-Performance Prototype:</strong> A playable prototype with technically complex core mechanics was created in 48 hours.</li>\n<li><strong>Optimization Task Solved:</strong> The system on <code>Compute Shader</code> allowed efficiently managing thousands of GPU instances and reading the result without performance loss.</li>\n<li><strong>Key Competency:</strong> The project proves the ability to <strong>integrate into someone else's code and extend it using advanced GPU programming techniques</strong> (<code>Compute Shaders</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n","published":true,"title":"Rhino Future","date":"2021-11","type":"project","tagsArray":["Unity","C#","Blender","Illustrator","HLSL","Compute Shaders","Hackathon"],"heroVideo":["ZEuHCmW7qE8"],"shortDescription":"<p>Selectel hackathon project: implemented a grass \"eating\" system by controlling thousands of instances in real-time using <mark>Compute Shaders</mark>.</p>\n","storeLinks":["https://selectel.ru/blog/retro-game-jam-21/"],"role":"solo","projectIcon":"/images/projects/21.11.RhinoFuture/icon.webp","cardBackground":"/images/projects/21.11.RhinoFuture/card.mp4?v=1765046976164","screenshots":[{"src":"/images/projects/21.11.RhinoFuture/screenshots/1.webp","width":1680,"height":944},{"src":"/images/projects/21.11.RhinoFuture/screenshots/2.webp","width":1680,"height":944},{"src":"/images/projects/21.11.RhinoFuture/screenshots/3.webp","width":1680,"height":944},{"src":"/images/projects/21.11.RhinoFuture/screenshots/4.webp","width":1680,"height":944},{"src":"/images/projects/21.11.RhinoFuture/screenshots/5.webp","width":1680,"height":944}]}